Rules:
  [R1] Use React Query for server state (caching, refetching).
  [R2] Use Zustand or Jotai for client state (UI state).
  [R3] Use Context API sparingly â€” only for truly global state.
  [R4] Use Redux Toolkit for complex state logic.
  [R5] Normalize state shape for relational data.
  [R6] Use selectors for derived state.
  [R7] Use optimistic updates for better UX.
  [R8] Use state machines (XState) for complex UI flows.

Pros:
  - Predictable state
  - Better debugging
  - Improved performance

Cons:
  - Added complexity
  - Learning curve
  - Boilerplate

Alternatives:
  - Vue Pinia
  - Angular NgRx
  - Svelte stores

